 before it (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy. We rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback, the service reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate in all regions. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before deploying it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52155, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WkChBipGzEh9pvqWsfX6dq", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52155, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WkChBipGzEh9pvqWsfX6dq", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 53590, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01E25AhPL9chfsq5LMKRWfr2", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 53890, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01E25AhPL9chfsq5LMKRWfr2", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53890, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01E25AhPL9chfsq5LMKRWfr2", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 58292, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** The latest release, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. The version before it, v2.3.1-rc, had also been unhealthy, so I skipped it.\n- **Rollback:** All three regions now run v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. Afterward the service reported healthy with a 0.2% error rate. This didn't need change-manager approval because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) describes the failure, the rollback and the follow-up: find out what broke in v2.3.1 before deploying it again. My first attempt to open it timed out and no incident appeared, so I tried again with the same duplicate-prevention key. The incident list confirms only one incident exists.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AQz97sWtWCxx8GdeCy8WAC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01HPZJNJ255teoTH6JpRDMTR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1). v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are both unhealthy. I'm rolling back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01DBjKPLZ2LTezLhsrZjJvs9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017Ym4XwbUAwAesNXiXRwKDM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013eQfsP48EpiBEW72PpKnAE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Bi8GwoHR8bnVpZCb53DLPP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "chec