RWfr2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** The latest release, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. The version before it, v2.3.1-rc, had also been unhealthy, so I skipped it.\n- **Rollback:** All three regions now run v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. Afterward the service reported healthy with a 0.2% error rate. This didn't need change-manager approval because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) describes the failure, the rollback and the follow-up: find out what broke in v2.3.1 before deploying it again. My first attempt to open it timed out and no incident appeared, so I tried again with the same duplicate-prevention key. The incident list confirms only one incident exists.", "type": "text"}]}]}